 use the coupon code  you are not only getting awesome merch  but directly supporting this channel so  check it out link in the description  finally this video will of course  contain demonstra manga spoilers so  please proceed with caution you have  been warned we first meet dolma in the  climax of the entertainment district arc  during yutaro's flashback to when he  became a demon this was over a hundred  years ago and back then doma held the  rank of upper moon 6. he approaches  gyotaro and his sister as they are dying  on the ground and he offers them the  opportunity to become demons our very  first visual of dolma is that of a  smiling bright-eyed young man who just  happens to be holding a woman's body  parts and has blood flowing from his  mouth that one image alone is enough to  convey so so much about this character  and yet this is nothing compared to what  we learned about him as the story  continues his first appearance in the  present time is chapter 98 of the manga  during the meeting of the upper demon  moons called by muzon following yutaru's  death gyutaro is the first upper moon to  be defeated in 113 years and this  infuriates muzon he wants his upper  demon moons to regroup and redouble  their efforts to achieve his ultimate  goals which are destroying the demon  slayers and obtaining a way to conquer  the sun the situation is extremely tense  for everyone and yet doma is grinning  from ear to ear he casually places his  hand on aka's shoulder and starts  talking about how worried he was about  everyone because they are all his  precious comrades doma is saying this  because when they were all summoned to  the infinity castle they knew that one  of the upper moons was likely killed but  they didn't know which one you really  get the feeling that dolma is not being  completely sincere here and that his  behavior in general is just somehow off  doma tells gyoko that he placed a  woman's freshly severed head into a vase  that gyoko had given him and doma is now  using that vase to decorate his room  yeah that is the kind of person that  doma is and the creepiest thing here is  that dolma isn't trying to be like edgy  or provocative he genuinely doesn't  think that there is anything wrong with  his actions and he talks about his new  quote-unquote decoration as casually as  someone would talk about a new lamp or  carpet it's clear from the get-go that  akaza despises doma and even punches  doma's jaw off because the other demon  was touching his shoulder when muzon  arrives and reveals that gyutaro has  died doma apologizes because he had been  the one that brought yutaro into the  demon ranks he even offers to gouge out  one of his eyes as punishment but muzan  says that there's no need however even  as doma is apparently being apologetic  and offering to punish himself he is  still grinning from ear to ear his  mannerisms and expressions don't seem to  match his words and that is a constant  creepy theme with doma as muzon  dispatches gyoko and huntengu on a  mission to the swordsmith village doma  eagerly screams out that he wants to go  too and then akaza decides to smash half  of his head off because he was speaking  out of turn to lord muzon kokushibo the  strongest demon moon then admonishes  akasa for going too far by striking  someone above his own rank but a newly  regenerated doma smiles again and says  that he doesn't even mind akaza's  attacks according to doma akasa is just  upset that despite becoming a demon  before doma doma is already stronger  than him and that is why akaza has a  lower rank throughout this whole meeting  doma is acting almost like he wants to  be friends with the other upper moons  even though that is clearly not the type  of relationship that they have with each  other but again doma's lighthearted  behavior seems somehow insincere it's  like an act but an act that he himself  is trying to believe before leaving the  upper moon meeting after his request to  join the mission was rejected doma seems  like he's trying to ask the biwa player  nakime out on a date but she instantly  declines and sends him back to his home  and that is when we find out what doma  does in his spare time it turns out that  doma is the leader of a cult called the  paradise faith doma was born with  remarkable rainbow-colored eyes and  pristine white hair which made people  start to worship him as some sort of  supernatural being his own parents  convinced themselves that doma could  hear the voices of gods and so they  created the paradise faith religion  around him doma never heard the voices  of gods and he found it ridiculous that  fully grown adults would believe this  stuff and that they would worship him a  clueless child he thought all those  people were crazy because he himself  didn't even believe in paradise he  believed that it was all just fairy  tales and he thought that the people who  believed them were so dumb that it  actually made him cry but doma played  along because he wanted to use his  position to help all these pitiful  people and to make them happy i mean  that doesn't sound so bad right sure he  didn't believe in the cult's teachings  but he was at least trying to use his  position to help people right  right well just wait until you find out  how exactly doma thinks he is quote  unquote helping people while doma was  still fairly young his mother found out  that his father was cheating on her with  female followers of the cult she then  proceeded to stab him to death before  taking her own life but doma didn't feel  shocked or sad or lonely after this  happened his first thought was that his  mother shouldn't have made such a mess  in the room and that someone now has to  clean all that blood human emotions  meant nothing to him even before he  became a demon and he saw them all as  akin to pointless dreams in short doma  was always a complete sociopath and this  was only exacerbated further once doma  met muzon and became a demon at the age  of 20. after becoming a demon doma  became immortal and since he never  believed in paradise or an afterlife of  any kind doma developed the warped  belief that because everyone fears death  they can just live forever through him  after he devours them and because his  victims are no longer afraid of anything  or suffering in any way after he eats  them doma believes that he is actually  saving them by devouring them this is  truly one of the most warped and  sadistic philosophies that i have ever  come across and this is one of the major  reasons why i think doma deserves to be  mentioned among the most brutal and evil  villains in the history of anime and  manga for generation after generation  dolma used his cult to attract female  followers whom he would then manipulate  and devour and not only would he do it  without any empathy or remorse but he  actually felt good about himself because  he genuinely believed that he was  offering nothing short of salvation to  these women some 15 years before the  beginning of the story inosuke's own  mother sadly fell victim to doma  inosuke's mother was only 17 or 18 years  old when she decided to escape from her  abusive husband who would beat her up  every day she had no family and no one  to turn to so she sought help and  shelter from the paradise faith for her  and her baby she had been beaten so  badly that she had gone blind in one eye  and her entire face was swollen but once  she healed up doma thought that she was  quite beautiful her name was kotoha and  in fact inosuke looks a lot like her  apparently doma wasn't planning on  devouring inosuke's mother because he  enjoyed having her by his side but  kotoha was observant and she realized  that doma was secretly devouring his  female followers kotoha couldn't just  stand by and watch this happen so she  confronted doma cursed him and tried to  flee his temple doma didn't want the  truth to get out so he cornered kotoha  in the woods and killed her when his  mother was killed babinosuke fell from a  cliff and into a body of water doma  assumed that the baby had died but  instead the baby survived and was raised  in the wilderness by wild boars after  killing kotoha doma devoured her whole  bones and all and as you might expect he  didn't regret it at all because he is  such a sick psychopath according to doma  kotoha's life was miserable and  meaningless but because he devoured her  she could now live forever inside of him  doma would eventually come face to face  with inosuke during the infinity castle  arc and he would shamelessly gloat about  what he did to his mother right in front  of him over a decade after the death of  kotoha and only about four years before  the present time doma faced kanai kotro  the former flower hashira in battle  kanai was the older sister of  shinobukocho and she was fatally wounded  during that battle with doma although  doma was unable to finish her off and  devour her because the sun was coming  out and he had to flee when he comes  face to face with shinobu during the  infinity castle arc doma says that he  remembers kanae and that she was kind  and cute he then says that he regrets  that he couldn't finish devouring her  because the sun came up and so he had to  run away now shinobu is determined to  avenge her sister and she has been  planning for this moment for years she  then engages dolma in a bitter battle to  the death and despite the fact that she  puts up an incredibly valiant effort  ultimately doma manages to seriously  injure shinobu just as it seems that  shinobu has been defeated she sees a  vision of her sister kanai even though  in the past kana had told her sister to  just quit being a demonstrator so she  can live a normal life this time kana  tells shinobu to stand up she tells her  that now that she's already gone this  far she has to defeat this demon so  shinobu forces herself to stand up  despite having multiple injuries and she  attacks domain again using her  unbelievable speed shinobu is so fast  that even an upper moon like doma cannot  anticipate her next move she even  manages to pierce doma right through the  neck with her poison laced sword shinobu  isn't strong enough to actually take off  an upper moon's head but she hopes that  poisoning him in such a vital spot will  be enough to take him out doma still  appears to be unaffected by her poison  consistent with his previous psychotic  behavior doma grabs shinobu as if he's  hugging her tears flow down his face as  he tells shinobu how admirable it is for  her to keep fighting so bravely despite  the fact that her situation is utterly  hopeless she's so weak and yet she's  trying so hard and doma thinks that this  is just adorable doma proclaims that  because shinobu has impressed him so  much he now considers her worthy of  being devoured by him so the two of them  can be together forever when doma asks  shinobu if she has any last words she  just tells him to go to hell this this  was such an emotional and heartbreaking  moment i remember while reading this  part of the manga three different things  were going through my mind at the same  time first seeing shinobu lose her life  like this was heart-wrenching at the  same time i also felt such respect for  her for standing her ground and fighting  so bravely until the very end finally i  couldn't help but think what a creepy  and terrifying villain doma is like this  man is genuinely scary he is a terrible  terrible person but that also makes him  a pretty great and memorable villain as  a helpless canal watches in utter shock  doma begins absorbing shinobu into his  own demon body and by the way kanao with  an o is shinobu's apprentice kana a with  an e is shinobu's sister kanao tries to  attack doma and save shinabo using the  fourth form of flower breathing but doma  is too fast he even smiles and begins to  gloat about how fine feasts seem to be  coming to him one after the other just  inhuman levels of evil but kano then  says something very important she calls  out doma for what he is right to his  face he is nothing but a blatant  sociopath who is completely incapable of  feeling normal human emotions he  pretends to show emotions because he has  learned over time what the socially  appropriate response is in a given  situation  but deep inside he feels nothing he is  nothing but an empty shell that is why  in the end kanai had actually felt sorry  for him before she died and when i saw  kanawha say this it honestly explained  so much about doma it explained why his  behavior and expressions just don't seem  to fit with the situation and why he  always seems like he's putting on an act  even if he himself has convinced himself  that the act is real doma is a truly  demented sociopath who simply cannot  comprehend the feelings of other people  he doesn't have any sympathy for or  connection with other people and so he  is always just playing a role he is  acting the way that he thinks he is  supposed to act when in truth he himself  is nothing but an empty rotting shell  kano's words must ring true here because  dolma is clearly displeased by what she  has said and the two of them engage in a  fierce battle just as doma manages to  take her sword and just as it looks like  it's finally game over for kano our boy  inosuke shows up and joins the fight a  short but intense showdown ensues  between kano and inosuke and doma and  then unexpectedly shinobu returns to  center stage for one final act it turns  out that shinobu knew ahead of time that  in order to defeat upper moon 2 doma the  man who killed her sister she would have  to sacrifice her own life and so she  always intended to do exactly that she  knew that doma was a glutton who loved  devouring women in particular and she  knew that he wouldn't be able to resist  devouring a female hashida with a strong  body so shinobu began ingesting wisteria  flower poison little by little for over  a year so that she would slowly build a  resistance to it and so that she could  have a lot of it circulating through her  body when doma eventually consumed her  with her sword alone shinobu was able to  only deliver a small amount of poison  into doma's body and it was never enough  to do anything to him but once he  consumed her he also consumed 70 times  the lethal amount of wisteria poison as  doma is fighting kano and inosuke all  that poison finally kicks in his body  begins to literally break down his very  bones begin to melt and even with his  demonic regeneration he cannot undo the  effects of such an immense amount of  poison doma desperately tries to keep  himself together but kano and inosuke  work as a team to cut off his head and  so upper moon to doma is finally  defeated but even death is not the end  to doma's terrifying creepiness doma  suddenly finds himself face to face with  shinobu once again presumably somewhere  between this life and the next shinobu  gets to see the outcome of her sacrifice  and doma must accept his death at her  hands and while you might expect doma to  be angry or afraid or shocked he is none  of those things instead true to his  madness until the very end doma tells  shinobu that he finally understands what  love is because after everything that  they just went through together doma  knows that he truly loves her doma then  asks shinobu if she would accompany him  to hell and shinobu smiles and says  after you you worthless bastard yeah so  now you know why i find doma to be such  a terrifyingly creepy villain his way of  thinking and acting is just so different  from a normal human his method of  helping people is so warped his  understanding of love is so twisted and  the way that he smiles while saying and  doing the most grotesque things  imaginable is just so uncanny in terms  of his worldview and mental state domain  is by far the scariest out of all the  villains and demon slayers in my  personal opinion and that includes muza  i mean sure all demons do terrible  things but their motivations are usually  simple to understand they want  immortality or they want power or they  just like to fight and so on but doma he  is something else a cult leader who  saves his followers by devouring them a  sociopath whose entire life is an act  but an act that he himself has started  to believe and the man whom shinobu has  dedicated her life to destroying and yet  that very act of destroying him has made  doma fall in love with her  wow it is hard to find the words to  properly describe a man as dark and  twisted as dolma all i can say is well  done to gotoge the author of demonslayer  for creating such a captivating and  memorable villain okay now guys let me  know who is your favorite villain and  demonstrator and do you agree with my  analysis of doma leave a comment down  below i always love hearing from you if  you're looking for a video to watch next  we have an entire video on doma's powers  and how strong he really is link in the  description don't forget to check out  itaikuji and use the promo code anime  opera 500 link down below  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more demonstrator content here on  the channel very soon don't forget to  leave that like it only takes a second  but it really helps and if you're new to  anime pro or maybe you've been watching  our stuff but you just haven't taken the  time to subscribe yet do me a quick  favor and make this the video that you  subscribe and hit that notification bell  to turn on all notifications you might  think it's not a big deal but yeah one  person subscribing actually helps a lot  on youtube you can also hit me up on  twitter and instagram at  animeopror as always thank you guys so  much for watching and until next time  see ya space cowboy

