 her  unbelievable speed shinobu is so fast  that even an upper moon like doma cannot  anticipate her next move she even  manages to pierce doma right through the  neck with her poison laced sword shinobu  isn't strong enough to actually take off  an upper moon's head but she hopes that  poisoning him in such a vital spot will  be enough to take him out doma still  appears to be unaffected by her poison  consistent with his previous psychotic  behavior doma grabs shinobu as if he's  hugging her tears flow down his face as  he tells shinobu how admirable it is for  her to keep fighting so bravely despite  the fact that her situation is utterly  hopeless she's so weak and yet she's  trying so hard and doma thinks that this  is just adorable doma proclaims that  because shinobu has impressed him so  much he now considers her worthy of  being devoured by him so the two of them  can be together forever when doma asks  shinobu if she has any last words she  just tells him to go to hell this this  was such an emotional and heartbreaking  moment i remember while reading this  part of the manga three different things  were going through my mind at the same  time first seeing shinobu lose her life  like this was heart-wrenching at the  same time i also felt such respect for  her for standing her ground and fighting  so bravely until the very end finally i  couldn't help but think what a creepy  and terrifying villain doma is like this  man is genuinely scary he is a terrible  terrible person but that also makes him  a pretty great and memorable villain as  a helpless canal watches in utter shock  doma begins absorbing shinobu into his  own demon body and by the way kanao with  an o is shinobu's apprentice kana a with  an e is shinobu's sister kanao tries to  attack doma and save shinabo using the  fourth form of flower breathing but doma  is too fast he even smiles and begins to  gloat about how fine feasts seem to be  coming to him one after the other just  inhuman levels of evil but kano then  says something very important she calls  out doma for what he is right to his  face he is nothing but a blatant  sociopath who is completely incapable of  feeling normal human emotions he  pretends to show emotions because he has  learned over time what the socially  appropriate response is in a given  situation  but deep inside he feels nothing he is  nothing but an empty shell that is why  in the end kanai had actually felt sorry  for him before she died and when i saw  kanawha say this it honestly explained  so much about doma it explained why his  behavior and expressions just don't seem  to fit with the situation and why he  always seems like he's putting on an act  even if he himself has convinced himself  that the act is real doma is a truly  demented sociopath who simply cannot  comprehend the feelings of other people  he doesn't have any sympathy for or  connection with other people and so he  is always just playing a role he is  acting the way that he thinks he is  supposed to act when in truth he himself  is nothing but an empty rotting shell  kano's words must ring true here because  dolma is clearly displeased by what she  has said and the two of them engage in a  fierce battle just as doma manages to  take her sword and just as it looks like  it's finally game over for kano our boy  inosuke shows up and joins the fight a  short but intense showdown ensues  between kano and inosuke and doma and  then unexpectedly shinobu returns to  center stage for one final act it turns  out that shinobu knew ahead of time that  in order to defeat upper moon 2 doma the  man who killed her sister she would have  to sacrifice her own life and so she  always intended to do exactly that she  knew that doma was a glutton who loved  devouring women in particular and she  knew that he wouldn't be able to resist  devouring a female hashida with a strong  body so shinobu began ingesting wisteria  flower poison little by little for over  a year so that she would slowly build a  resistance to it and so that she could  have a lot of it circulating through her  body when doma eventually consumed her  with her sword alone shinobu was able to  only deliver a small amount of poison  into doma's body and it was never enough  to do anything to him but once he  consumed her he also consumed 70 times  the lethal amount of wisteria poison as  doma is fighting kano and inosuke all  that poison finally kicks in his body  begins to literally break down his very  bones begin to melt and even with his  demonic regeneration he cannot undo the  effects of such an immense amount of  poison doma desperately tries to keep  himself together but kano and inosuke  work as a team to cut off his head and  so upper moon to doma is finally  defeated but even death is not the end  to doma's terrifying creepiness doma  suddenly finds himself face to face with  shinobu once again presumably somewhere  between this life and the next shinobu  gets to see the outcome of her sacrifice  and doma must accept his death at her  hands and while you might expect doma to  be angry or afraid or shocked he is none  of those things instead true to his  madness until the very end doma tells  shinobu that he finally understands what  love is because after everything that  they just went through together doma  knows that he truly loves her doma then  asks shinobu if she would accompany him  to hell and shinobu smiles and says  after you you worthless bastard yeah so  now you know why i find doma to be such  a terrifyingly creepy villain his way of  thinking and acting is just so different  from a normal human his method of  helping people is so warped his  understanding of love is so twisted and  the way that he smiles while saying and  doing the most grotesque things  imaginable is just so uncanny in terms  of his worldview and mental state domain  is by far the scariest out of all the  villains and demon slayers in my  personal opinion and that includes muza  i mean sure all demons do terrible  things but their motivations are usually  simple to understand they want  immortality or they want power or they  just like to fight and so on but doma he  is something else a cult leader who  saves his followers by devouring them a  sociopath whose entire life is an act  but an act that he himself has started  to believe and the man whom shinobu has  dedicated her life to destroying and yet  that very act of destroying him has made  doma fall in love with her  wow it is hard to find the words to  properly describe a man as dark and  twisted as dolma all i can say is well  done to gotoge the author of demonslayer  for creating such a captivating and  memorable villain okay now guys let me  know who is your favorite villain and  demonstrator and do you agree with my  analysis of doma leave a comment down  below i always love hearing from you if  you're looking for a video to watch next  we have an entire video on doma's powers  and how strong he really is link in the  description don't forget to check out  itaikuji and use the promo code anime  opera 500 link down below  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more demonstrator content here on  the channel very soon don't forget to  leave that like it only takes a second  but it really helps and if you're new to  anime pro or maybe you've been watching  our stuff but you just haven't taken the  time to subscribe yet do me a quick  favor and make this the video that you  subscribe and hit that notification bell  to turn on all notifications you might  think it's not a big deal but yeah one  person subscribing actually helps a lot  on youtube you can also hit me up on  twitter and instagram at  animeopror as always thank you guys so  much for watching and until next time  see ya space cowboy
 

